WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.925 --> 00:00:04.175
Reaching orbit takes speed as well as
height.

2
00:00:04.225 --> 00:00:07.075
What if the machinery that gives a payload
that speed

3
00:00:07.125 --> 00:00:08.825
could stay in space?

4
00:00:10.275 --> 00:00:13.625
A skyhook is a rotating tether in orbit.

5
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:15.425
Near the bottom of its swing,

6
00:00:15.475 --> 00:00:18.175
the tip moves against the orbital motion,

7
00:00:18.225 --> 00:00:22.425
reducing the speed an approaching payload
needs to match.

8
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:27.275
In this concept, a hypersonic aircraft
climbs,

9
00:00:27.325 --> 00:00:29.600
then coasts toward the moving tip.

10
00:00:29.675 --> 00:00:32.850
Position, speed and timing must align.

11
00:00:32.925 --> 00:00:34.950
A grapple secures the payload,

12
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.150
and the tether carries the load.

13
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.200
The tether lifts the payload and releases
it

14
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.675
onto a higher-energy trajectory.

15
00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:47.100
After release, it coasts under gravity.

16
00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:51.175
That energy comes from the tether's
motion.

17
00:00:51.225 --> 00:00:54.775
Propulsion, or carefully planned returning
cargo,

18
00:00:54.825 --> 00:00:57.375
could restore what the outgoing payload
took

19
00:00:57.425 --> 00:00:59.275
before the next delivery.

20
00:01:00.725 --> 00:01:05.075
At the Moon, a mass driver could launch
cargo toward a lunavator.

21
00:01:05.125 --> 00:01:07.750
The payload accelerates along the track,

22
00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.000
then coasts to the grapple.

23
00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:14.800
Phobos itself could anchor the network at
Mars.

24
00:01:14.875 --> 00:01:17.500
Mercury could support solar industry.

25
00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:22.100
And a mission to comet Finlay could put a
source of water within reach.

26
00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:26.300
Try a guided flight in Flight Studio.

27
00:01:26.375 --> 00:01:29.300
Build and supply a network in Expeditions.

28
00:01:29.375 --> 00:01:30.900
Start with one handoff,

29
00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:32.850
and see where it could lead.
